# Units masked on the image, as symlinks to /dev/null. Same reason as
# services.enable: git on Windows cannot check out a symlink, so the list is
# text and scripts/build-iso.sh makes the links on the Linux build host.
#
# plymouth-quit tears the splash down at the end of boot, which is several
# seconds before Hyprland and the launcher have drawn anything — exactly the
# black gap the splash exists to cover. omni-launcher quits plymouth itself
# once it is on screen, and omnios-splash-guard.service is the backstop.
plymouth-quit.service
# plymouth-quit-wait blocks multi-user.target until plymouth exits. Masking
# only plymouth-quit leaves nothing to make it exit, so boot deadlocks behind
# the splash: no getty, no autologin, no launcher, and a black tty2. Both have
# to go, and omnios-splash-guard becomes the only thing that ends the splash if
# the launcher never starts.
plymouth-quit-wait.service
